{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463138",
      "title": "Binding Attributes with the \"v-bind\" Directive",
      "lectureOrder": 18,
      "videoOrder": 14,
      "sourceHash": "7881b984da41b3b566f51554667a26ac6db8815ac8404e566b535a23b082c2f7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 5.5,
          "en": "Now we covered two super important features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.5,
          "end": 9.22,
          "en": "How we create a Vue instance and configure the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.22,
          "end": 10.41,
          "en": "that we can use there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.41,
          "end": 13.48,
          "en": "and how we can output data with interpolation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.48,
          "end": 17.35,
          "en": "Now, you don't always want to use interpolation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.35,
          "end": 18.98,
          "en": "for outputting data, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.98,
          "end": 20.163,
          "en": "Here's an example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.03,
          "end": 23.257,
          "en": "Let's say we have a second paragraph, where I say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.257,
          "end": 26.8,
          "en": "\"learn more about Vue\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.8,
          "end": 30.12,
          "en": "and I want to make sure that \"about Vue\" is a link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.12,
          "end": 33.37,
          "en": "Of course we can use a anchor tag with the ref attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.37,
          "end": 37.14,
          "en": "for that, and wrap that around \"about Vue\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.14,
          "end": 39.08,
          "en": "If I do that, this is what we get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.08,
          "end": 42.193,
          "en": "And now in here, we can pass in our link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.92,
          "end": 47.93,
          "en": "Now, just as before, we could absolutely hard code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.93,
          "end": 51.34,
          "en": "this here in our HTML code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.34,
          "end": 56.34,
          "en": "but let's again store the link value in our Vue app instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.76,
          "end": 61.94,
          "en": "and then add some syntax to output the stored value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.94,
          "end": 64.82,
          "en": "simply so that later in the next step, we can make this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.82,
          "end": 66.7,
          "en": "a bit more dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.7,
          "end": 69.33,
          "en": "So for that, I'm going to add a second property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.33,
          "end": 72.47,
          "en": "to this object which is returned in data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.47,
          "end": 73.937,
          "en": "and I'll name it \"vueLink\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.86,
          "end": 78.7,
          "en": "And now this again is a string that can lead to a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.7,
          "end": 81.67,
          "en": "where you can learn more about Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.67,
          "end": 84.95,
          "en": "Now here, I'm simply going to use the official Vue webpage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.95,
          "end": 87.94,
          "en": "but again you can of course use anything here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.94,
          "end": 91.61,
          "en": "Now, this vueLink property now holds the link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.61,
          "end": 95.02000000000001,
          "en": "that should be output here, and we can of course try",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.02000000000001,
          "end": 98.14,
          "en": "to use our curly braces here, just as we did it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.14,
          "end": 100.53,
          "en": "between the paragraph tags, now I'm doing this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.53,
          "end": 103.03999999999999,
          "en": "on the ref attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.03999999999999,
          "end": 105.52000000000001,
          "en": "So here we then point at vueLink,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.52000000000001,
          "end": 109.2,
          "en": "save this, reload, and click \"about Vue\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.2,
          "end": 112.83,
          "en": "as you see, this fails, and, why does it fail,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.83,
          "end": 114.5,
          "en": "well, let's inspect this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.5,
          "end": 116.91,
          "en": "with the browser developer tools real quick,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.91,
          "end": 119.57,
          "en": "I'm using Chrome here, where you can right click something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.57,
          "end": 122.21,
          "en": "to inspect it, and you will see that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.21,
          "end": 125.98,
          "en": "the value for the ref attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.98,
          "end": 130.79,
          "en": "is actually the unconverted double curly brace syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.79,
          "end": 134.09,
          "en": "So clearly Vue did not replace this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.09,
          "end": 136.95,
          "en": "with the actual value stored in vueLink,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.95,
          "end": 140.34,
          "en": "as it did it before for this course goal part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.34,
          "end": 142.63,
          "en": "Now why did Vue not do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.63,
          "end": 146.57999999999998,
          "en": "We are inside of the Vue controlled HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.57999999999998,
          "end": 148.653,
          "en": "So Vue should detect this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.73,
          "end": 151.12,
          "en": "Well, the reason is simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.12,
          "end": 155.44,
          "en": "This double curly brace syntax is only available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.44,
          "end": 158.6,
          "en": "between opening and closing HTML tags, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.6,
          "end": 163.6,
          "en": "So anywhere, where you would, well, output actual content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.72,
          "end": 168.07,
          "en": "If you wanna pass in a dynamic value to an attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.07,
          "end": 172.4,
          "en": "like here, where I wanna set the value of the ref attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.4,
          "end": 175.59,
          "en": "dynamically with help of Vue, we need to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.59,
          "end": 179.26,
          "en": "a different syntax, which thankfully is available though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.26,
          "end": 183.12,
          "en": "And that's the Vue binding syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.12,
          "end": 186.15,
          "en": "For that, we use a so called vue directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.15,
          "end": 188.35,
          "en": "which is simply an extra instruction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.35,
          "end": 191.07,
          "en": "we add in the HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.07,
          "end": 194.76,
          "en": "And we can use such directives on HTML elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 194.76,
          "end": 197.24,
          "en": "like on this anchor element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 197.24,
          "end": 200.94,
          "en": "The directive we need here is v-bind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 200.94,
          "end": 205.19,
          "en": "V-bind is a reserved name, detected and understood by Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.19,
          "end": 207.59,
          "en": "and you can tell that it's by Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 207.59,
          "end": 210.13,
          "en": "because it starts with \"v-\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.13,
          "end": 213.53,
          "en": "All built in directives which ship with Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.53,
          "end": 216.06,
          "en": "start with \"v-\", and we're going to see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 216.06,
          "end": 218.51,
          "en": "a couple of other ones too throughout the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 219.44,
          "end": 223.17000000000002,
          "en": "Now, what does this v-bind directive do?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 223.17000000000002,
          "end": 226.66,
          "en": "As I said, a directive is basically an instruction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 226.66,
          "end": 229.97,
          "en": "An instruction we give to Vue to do something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.97,
          "end": 234.97,
          "en": "And v-bind tells Vue to bind, so to set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 235.15,
          "end": 237.2,
          "en": "the value of something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.2,
          "end": 239.86,
          "en": "and the \"of something\" part basically just means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.86,
          "end": 243.58,
          "en": "of an attribute on an HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.58,
          "end": 247.88,
          "en": "And to let Vue know which attribute's value to set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 247.88,
          "end": 250.41,
          "en": "we add a colon after v-bind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.41,
          "end": 253.24,
          "en": "and then the attribute name, in this case ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 253.24,
          "end": 256.68,
          "en": "and this is the full syntax which vue will understand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.68,
          "end": 261.68,
          "en": "to dynamically set a value of an HTML element attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 261.76,
          "end": 263.82,
          "en": "in this case of the ref attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 263.82,
          "end": 267.86,
          "en": "This tells Vue, please find, please set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.86,
          "end": 271.12,
          "en": "the value of the ref attribute to something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 271.12,
          "end": 273.18,
          "en": "and now the \"to something\" is passed between",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 273.18,
          "end": 275.55,
          "en": "the opening and closing double quotes here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 275.55,
          "end": 279.62,
          "en": "and here again, you can now reference a value of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 279.62,
          "end": 283.65999999999997,
          "en": "your data object, so in this case, vueLink for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 283.65999999999997,
          "end": 284.98,
          "en": "just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 284.98,
          "end": 288.4,
          "en": "So this here, v-bind, is basically, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 288.4,
          "end": 292.94,
          "en": "the attribute alternative to this interpolation syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 292.94,
          "end": 295.88,
          "en": "You use interpolation between HTML tags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.88,
          "end": 299.19,
          "en": "and if you need to set the value on an HTML tag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 299.19,
          "end": 301.07,
          "en": "so, to an attribute like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 301.07,
          "end": 302.64,
          "en": "you use v-bind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 302.64,
          "end": 304.401,
          "en": "If you now save this and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.401,
          "end": 308.17,
          "en": "we now click this link, I'm taken to the Vue docks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 308.17,
          "end": 311.92,
          "en": "So I'm basically forwarded to the page this link points at.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 311.92,
          "end": 315.7,
          "en": "So now this works, and v-bind, just like interpolation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 315.7,
          "end": 318,
          "en": "is a key feature you need to know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 318,
          "end": 321.07,
          "en": "because typically, you don't just want to output content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 321.07,
          "end": 322.98,
          "en": "between opening and closing tags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 322.98,
          "end": 326.31,
          "en": "often you have the scenario that you need to bind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 326.31,
          "end": 330.32,
          "en": "that you need to set the value of some HTML attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 330.32,
          "end": 334.12,
          "en": "to some Vue managed data, and with v-bind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 334.12,
          "end": 335.703,
          "en": "that's very easy to do.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
